<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise id="_56da4227-4773-4148-ad83-e42e2702a677" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-3)^2+10=9+10=19\)</para><para>The correct answer is 19. \((-3)^2+10=9+10=19\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="da7dc977-a70d-460f-8c68-b85042fe7f9b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-2)^2+10=4+10=14\)</para><para>The correct answer is 14. \((-2)^2+10=4+10=14\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_5ecbe22e-6069-44b9-aa7d-9ee9a27d0244" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-1)^2+10=1+10=11\)</para><para>The correct answer is 11. \((-1)^2+10=1+10=11\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="e52fa14f-0bad-44e3-a59d-807f4583fc09" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((0)^2+10=0+10=10\)</para><para>The correct answer is 10. \((0)^2+10=0+10=10\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="b634d6bc-9e5d-48cc-920b-2d8885844aec" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((1)^2+10=1+10=11\)</para><para>The correct answer is 11. \((1)^2+10=1+10=11\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="ee69e6ea-32ff-4701-9748-be0dd653d934" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((2)^2+10=4+10=14\)</para><para>The correct answer is 14. \((2)^2+10=4+10=14\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="b0b9ca01-0aaf-4afc-8fda-f32204c05a8d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((3)^2+10=9+10=19\)</para><para>The correct answer is 19. \((3)^2+10=9+10=19\)</para></solution></exercise></section>
