<section><exercise id="_414a4c79-f8ca-4d84-bdb0-3799b2d22150" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-3)^2-3=9-3=6\)</para><para>The correct answer is 6. \((-3)^2-3=9-3=6\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="f903c1c9-b5cf-482c-a4ca-22c9fa11ad99" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-2)^2-3=4-3=1\)</para><para>The correct answer is 1. \((-2)^2-3=4-3=1\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_9da988cd-6c24-4c40-b6ec-1f4ee1a64054" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-1)^2-3=1-3=-2\)</para><para>The correct answer is -2. \((-1)^2-3=1-3=-2\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="e7496405-bc12-4bc9-adcf-b73b9aec4f83" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((0)^2-3=0-3=-3\)</para><para>The correct answer is -3. \((0)^2-3=0-3=-3\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a09868fb-17d3-46d0-b856-6287faee4786" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2. (1)2-3=1-3=-2\)</para><para>The correct answer is -2. \(-2. (1)2-3=1-3=-2\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_29189482-f312-4e41-9f3b-fbf3c52bb5ef" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((2)^2-3=4-3=1\)</para><para>The correct answer is 1. \((2)^2-3=4-3=1\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_36a5a0df-8eed-4890-974e-47533bc33e7c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((3)^2-3=9-3=6\)</para><para>The correct answer is 6. \((3)^2-3=9-3=6\)</para></solution></exercise></section>
