<section><exercise id="_1ef18c42-7b66-4440-b804-f22f26238680" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(-3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para><para>The correct answer is -18. \(-2(-3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_49a47e47-fe91-40f5-8b9c-f7e12aa93cb7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(-2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para><para>The correct answer is -8. \(-2(-2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="de9fc74b-58ce-4763-bb13-43ffae05b658" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(-1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para><para>The correct answer is -2. \(-2(-1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_6f548ba3-e63f-4dc7-85a0-e84b52b5bae7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(0)^2=-2 \cdot 0=0\)</para><para>The correct answer is 0. \(-2(0)^2=-2 \cdot 0=0\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7cdbb75f-e4db-4503-9a20-d0cd22ce4d2f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para><para>The correct answer is -2. \(-2(1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_2bdcc76e-34cf-47ad-a401-e3883a0314a3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para><para>The correct answer is -8. \(-2(2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_246cb693-cf66-408c-b773-b892056f5dcf" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para/><para> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-2(3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para><para>The correct answer is -18.\(-2(3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para></solution></exercise></section>
<exercise>
  <problem> 
    <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to see the solutions to questions 4 – 6 organized into a table.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00007">
